{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman from the Crusader states in the Levant He was born around 1140 and died in 1187 He was the count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187 He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem He was also the nephew of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem\n\nRaymond III was married twice first to Constance of Antioch and then to Eschiva of Saint Omer They had no children together\n\nIn 1152 Raymond III became count of Tripoli after his father's death He was only a child at the time and his mother Hodierna served as regent until he came of age\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states in the Levant He was involved in the defense of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the Second Crusade in 1148 He also participated in the Battle of Harim in 1164 and the Battle of Artah in 1165\n\n*Highlighted section part 1: The Second Crusade*\n\nThe Second Crusade was a military expedition that took place in the mid-12th century It was called by Pope Eugene III in response to the fall of the County of Edessa to the Muslims in 1144 The Crusaders, led by King Louis VII of France and Emperor Conrad III of Germany, attempted to recapture Edessa but were unsuccessful\n\nRaymond III played a role in the defense of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the Second Crusade He fought in the Battle of Harim in 1164 and the Battle of Artah in 1165\n\n*Highlighted section part 2: The Battle of Harim*\n\nThe Battle of Harim was fought in 1164 between the Crusaders and the Muslims It took place near the city of Harim in modern-day Syria The Crusaders were led by Raymond III and the Muslims by Nur al-Din The Crusaders were defeated and Raymond III was captured by the Muslims\n\nRaymond III was held captive by Nur al-Din for several years before being released in a prisoner exchange in 1173\n\n*Highlighted section part 3: The Battle of Artah*\n\nThe Battle of Artah was fought in 1165 between the Crusaders and the Muslims It took place near the city of Artah in modern-day Syria The Crusaders were led by Raymond III and the Muslims by Nur al-Din The Crusaders were victorious in this battle\n\nRaymond III continued to serve as count of Tripoli until his death in 1187 He was succeeded by his cousin Bohemond III\n\nIn conclusion Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a significant figure in the history of the Crusader states in the Levant He played a role in the defense of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the Second Crusade and was involved in several battles against the Muslims He was the count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187 He was married twice but had no children with either of his wives.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -3.9219088648678735e-05}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.0001627074379939586}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.3794739544391632}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -8.940656698541716e-06}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -1.015670657157898}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.15181967616081238}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -0.06262174993753433}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.0029099523089826107}, {"token": "from", "logprob": -1.1415737867355347}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "Cr", "logprob": -0.5246592164039612}, {"token": "us", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "states", "logprob": -0.035062067210674286}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.07649440318346024}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0001174142598756589}, {"token": "Lev", "logprob": -0.0049157715402543545}, {"token": "ant", "logprob": -7.521823135903105e-05}, {"token": "He", "logprob": -0.025257889181375504}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.0002901133266277611